# Lifetime regions and escape validation

One lifetime owner, retained-edge legality, escape validation and region topology.

## Contract

- Input: validated HIR, borrow facts, function lifetime/effect summaries, external boundary profiles, reactive observability facts, and builder-supplied lifecycle roots
- Output: immutable lifetime-region, allocation-family, retained-edge, escape, cycle, outlives, non-lexical interval, retained-edge liveness and cleanup-frontier candidates
- Decides: semantic lifetime ownership and topology legality
- Must not decide: source access syntax, HIR shape, target partition, physical memory strategy, handle-tag encoding, REC selection, or backend lowering
- Invariant: any physical representation, garbage-collected or not, may realise only a topology already proven legal

Inferred regions are compiler-generated non-lexical CFG intervals. This analysis also owns retained-edge liveness and final cleanup frontiers, which let a region end before the aggregate that once held its values. Those facts decide reclamation precision, never legality.

Implementation of this analysis is deferred. Canonical grouped-memory semantics live under `docs/src/docs/codebase/memory-management/declared-memory-groups/`. The roadmap file owns implementation sequencing and deferred follow-up only.

